<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13894" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diffundĭto</span></b> ,
		āre, v. freq. a.
		diffundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to pour out, scatter, spread</i> (very rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perh. only post-class.): pretium per domos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 18, 5, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid ex sese,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 21, 1, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubique sese diffunditans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 16, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amoris vi diffunditari ac didier,</span>”
				<i>to be consumed, wasted</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. prol. 54</span></i>
			.</div>
